..and now I have checked some more patches for 3.4.3 compatibility.

The color HP monitor didn't need to be changed because the whole botl.c is
identical in 3.4.2 and 3.4.3. But because there was "342" in the file
name, I made a new diff.

The showscore_hide only needed to be rediffed because of some line in the
context had been changed. The patch hides the SCORE_ON_BOTL option from
the bones and save files, so you can have the option on even if you use
hearse or otherwise exchange bones with people who use the official
source.

The forgetquit patch prevents quit games to be written in the record file
and prompts for writing wizard and debug mode games to the logfile.
This one only had some line numbers changed from 3.4.2.

The germankb patch swaps the commands for the y and z keys around, so
people with a German keyboard can have the Northwest movement command
between t and u like the rest of us.
Only line numbers changed from 3.4.2 here too.

All these patches can be downloaded from 
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html

(And now the deathexplore patch is the only platform-independent one of my
 own patches that I haven't yet checked with 3.4.3..)

